-- title:
--   Formal smoothness of the blow-up chart C[J/varpiₜ]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$.
--
--   **Base data.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ (Laurent series over $L$), and `hK` pins it down as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H$ with $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ and $H =$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with algebra structures making $L$ its fraction field and $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and has Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the image in $L((t))$ of the $q$-expansion $t^{-1} + 744 + \cdots$ of the modular $j$-invariant. Further, $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$, and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **The chart algebra and the supersingular point.** Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A K j` $= j$. The ideal $y \subseteq C$ is maximal, contains $\varpi$, and satisfies the supersingularity hypothesis `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Let $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two morphisms from the middle chart to $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. The point $z \in X$ is such that the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi \in A$ (this is `hϖz`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hz`); $y'$ is a point of `XFin` $= \operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` mapping $y'$ to $z$ (`hy'`), the same supersingularity condition `hss'` holds for ring homomorphisms out of $C$ with kernel $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and `hy'y` states $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart witness.** $W_1$ is a complete discrete valuation domain, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, and $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`). Put
--   $$S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})\,v_1 - f_1u_1\bigr),$$
--   with quotient map $\mathrm{mk}_S$, and let $e_1$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion `CMP` of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S$; $\mathrm{toC}$ denotes the map from the stalk to its completion and $\mathrm{germ}_Y : C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ the germ map at $z$ through the finite chart.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses, summarised here. (W1) For every $a \in A$, $e_1$ carries the image of $a$ in the completed stalk to the class of the constant $\sigma_1 a$. (W2) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — which says that for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, with $p_g$ having non-zero image, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\delta = \begin{pmatrix}\delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/m\\ m\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$. (W3) If moreover $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, the restriction of such a $\tau$ to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. (W4) For $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W_1$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{M}_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines the action of $\tau$ on $C$ with the identification $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y$, $\theta$ fixes all constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity. (W5) For integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each containing the class of $\sigma_1\varpi$, each omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, and each containing some element $a_k X_0 + b_k X_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to the stalk along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct. (W6) For a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $\sigma_1\varpi$ and containing an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for $a \in C$: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$. (W7) The element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the $(q\ell)$-fold $q$-expansion rescaling of the $j$-invariant series, lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference of this element and $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b \in W_1$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ the value $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e_1$ sends the image of that difference under $\mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y$ to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The centre and the chart.** The ideal $J \subseteq C$ is, by `hJ`, the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ of $C$ for which there exist $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying the same level condition for $\gamma^{-1}$ and mapping $C$ into $C$, such that $J'$ is the pullback along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$.
--
--   Finally, $B$ is an $A$-subalgebra of $K$ with, by `hB`, $B$ the restriction of scalars to $A$ of the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$; that is, $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** $B$ is a formally smooth $A$-algebra: `Algebra.FormallySmooth A ↥B`.
--
--   This is the formal-smoothness assertion about the weighted blow-up chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra along the centre $J$ cut out by the Drinfeld-type local description of the stalk at a supersingular point. It is used in the assembly of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_blowupChart_eq_adjoin_exceptionalValuation_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_stalk_drinfeldChart_moduliHasse`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_blowupChart_eq_adjoin_exceptionalValuation_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_stalk_drinfeldChart_moduliHasse), where the blow-up chart supplies the exceptional valuation on the auxiliary level structure; the two fibrewise formal-smoothness results over the closed and the generic point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$, together with finiteness of type of the chart algebras, feed into it.
